22. ONLINE AND OFFLINE WORKFLOWS

22.1 Member Registration Workflow

Authorized user creates member record.


Generate unique Member ID.


Upload photo and signature.


Assign registered mobile number.


Set or reset PIN securely.


Synchronize record.


Member can log in after account activation.


22.2 Saving Workflow

Authorized officer selects member.


Enter monthly saving.


Enter interest.


Enter fine.


Enter payment information.


Calculate total.


Save transaction locally or online.


Generate appropriate receipt.


If offline, add to pending synchronization queue.


Synchronize when online.


Update official financial ledger after server validation.


22.3 Loan Workflow

Member submits application.


Application appears in authorized approval dashboard.


President or authorized officer reviews it.


Application is approved or rejected.


Approved amount is recorded.


Actual loan disbursement is recorded separately.


Loan Register is updated.


Installments are recorded.


Remaining balance is calculated.


Receipt is generated.


Offline loan applications may be saved locally and submitted later.

22.4 Online Payment Workflow

Member opens payment page.


System displays active QR.


Member pays using supported UPI app.


Member enters Transaction ID.


Member uploads screenshot.


Payment enters Pending status.


Authorized officer verifies online.


Verified payment creates the corresponding ledger entry.


Receipt is generated.


Prevent duplicate posting.

Offline payment submissions remain Pending until verification.

22.5 Cash Book Workflow

Authorized officer records deposit or payment.


Calculate Bank and Cash balances separately.


Save transaction.


Update dashboard after successful posting.


Record audit entry.


Offline entries remain Pending until server validation.

22.6 Permission Workflow

System changes permission.


Save permission.


Backend enforces new permission.


Frontend navigation updates.


Offline permission cache refreshes during the next authenticated synchronization.


22.7 Offline Synchronization Workflow

User creates an authorized offline record.


Record is saved in IndexedDB.


Record receives a unique Operation ID.


Sync Status becomes Pending.


User sees the Pending count.


Internet becomes available.


Backend validates identity and permissions.


Backend checks duplicate Operation ID.


Backend validates all financial fields.


Backend saves the official record.


IndexedDB updates Sync Status to Synced.


Dashboard refreshes.


If synchronization fails, preserve the local record and show the reason.

